The larger cap is a reasonable candidate for the next pilot, but the old p95 cannot establish that it will be sufficient. I also found two details to pin down: parser precedence must preserve the final-answer rule, and calibration PLAN statistics include capped calls even though the profile usage table uses SOLVEs only.
